IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mig-prot-dates`

-- Migration Act 1958 (Cth) -- baseline encoding from the seat of the person seeking asylum in Australia: the applicant
-- for a protection visa, and the person whose protection visa is refused or cancelled, who asks the Administrative
-- Review Tribunal (ART) for review, and who faces removal.
--
-- SEAT. The asylum seeker (the protection visa applicant). Questions are phrased as that person asks them: "Am I a
-- refugee?", "Can I apply?", "By when must I apply to the ART?", "Can I be sent back to the country I fear?". The
-- Minister, the officer, the ASIO, the ART and the Parliament get no seat: their satisfactions, opinions, assessments
-- and determinations are asked as facts ("the Minister is satisfied that ...", "the Minister has serious reasons for
-- considering that ...").
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, a date, a list of dates, a choice from a list, or a record of such facts).
-- No question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT. The two duties with a deadline (s 347(3): my application to the ART;
-- reg 4.31B(2): my ART fee) are regulative rules run inside a question.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Act: s 5AAA (my responsibility for my claim); s 5AA(1), (1A), (3) (unauthorised maritime
-- arrival); s 5H (refugee); s 5J (well-founded fear of persecution); s 5L (particular social group); s 5LA (effective
-- protection measures); s 5M (particularly serious crime, as a choice); s 36(1A)-(5A) (the Act's criteria for a
-- protection visa: security, danger, refugee, complementary protection, family unit, a right to live in another
-- country); s 36A (the protection finding is considered first); s 46A(1), (1A), (2) (unauthorised maritime arrivals);
-- ss 48A, 48B (no further protection visa application); ss 91C, 91D, 91E, 91F (safe third countries); ss 91J, 91K, 91L
-- (temporary safe haven visas); s 91V(1)-(3) (oral statement on oath); ss 91W, 91WA (identity documents); s 91WB (family
-- applicants); ss 197C(3)-(9), 197D(6) (removal to the country I fear, and when a decision ending that protection is
-- complete); ss 338A, 347, 347A, 348 (ART review of a protection decision, who may apply, by when); s 368(7) and
-- ss 379A, 379C, 494B, 494C (when I am taken to have received the decision).
-- Regulations: reg 2.16(3) (a refusal is notified by a s 494B method); reg 4.31B (the ART fee and when it is paid).
--
-- Edition: Migration Act 1958, Compilation No. 171, compilation date 4 June 2026 (register id C2026C00232), as deposited
-- at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1958A00062.txt (retrieved 2026-09-22). Migration Regulations 1994 (F1996B03551),
-- Compilation No. 289, compilation date 2 October 2026 (register id F2026C01017), as deposited at
-- ../../../migration-regulations-1994/registers/source-bundle/F1996B03551.txt (retrieved 2026-10-20).
--
-- NOT ENCODED (see NOTES.md): s 5K (family as a social group: which fears to disregard); the Schedule 2 criteria for
-- the protection visa subclasses (asked as one fact); Part 5 procedure (hearings, invitations, decisions on the papers),
-- s 349 remittal orders, s 500 review; character (s 501); detention and the duty to remove (ss 189-198); ministerial
-- intervention; s 46B (transitory persons); s 91G (transitional applications); ss 91X, 91Y (publication); the indexed
-- ART fee (reg 4.31BA, 4.31BB: an input).
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. Answers follow the rulings on negatives of 2026-11-04 and
-- 2026-11-05 (NOTES.md): JUST FALSE is the text's own no; NOTHING is where the text is silent or limited by its own
-- wording.

§ `Migration Act 1958 -- the asylum seeker's questions`

DECLARE `Protection party` IS ONE OF `I, the applicant`
DECLARE `Protection step` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the ART for review`
    `pay the ART review fee`

-- Small helpers on MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN m IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is yes` m IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN JUST b THEN b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is no` m IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN JUST b THEN (NOT b)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

GIVEN m IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is open` m IF
    CONSIDER m
    WHEN JUST b THEN FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

§§ `s 5AAA -- whose job is it to make out my claim`

-- s 5AAA(2): "it is the responsibility of the non-citizen to specify all particulars of his or her claim to be such a
-- person and to provide sufficient evidence to establish the claim." (4): the Minister has no responsibility "to specify,
-- or assist in specifying, any particulars" or "establish, or assist in establishing, the claim".
@export Is it up to me to set out every detail of my claim for protection and to give enough evidence to prove it (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 5AAA)? Yes, if you claim that Australia owes you protection obligations: the Minister does not have to help you specify or establish the claim.
GIVEN `I claim protection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you claim that Australia owes you protection obligations (for example by applying for a protection visa)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it up to me to make out my claim question` `I claim protection` IF `I claim protection`

§§ `ss 5H, 5J, 5L, 5LA -- am I a refugee`

-- s 5J(4)(b): the persecution "must involve serious harm to the person". s 5J(5): "Without limiting what is serious
-- harm ..., the following are instances of serious harm": (a)-(f). The list is not closed: harm of another kind may
-- still be serious harm, which the Act does not say. So: JUST TRUE for a listed instance, NOTHING otherwise.
DECLARE `Harm I fear` IS ONE OF
    `a threat to my life or liberty`
    `significant physical harassment`
    `significant physical ill-treatment`
    `significant economic hardship that threatens my capacity to subsist`
    `denial of access to basic services that threatens my capacity to subsist`
    `denial of capacity to earn a livelihood of any kind that threatens my capacity to subsist`
    `harm of another kind`

GIVEN `the harm` IS A `Harm I fear`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5J(5) -- serious harm` `the harm` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the harm`
    WHEN `harm of another kind` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@export Is the harm I fear "serious harm", as persecution must involve (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 5J(4)(b), (5))? The Act lists six instances: a threat to life or liberty, significant physical harassment or ill-treatment, and economic hardship, denial of basic services or denial of any livelihood that threatens your capacity to subsist. The list does not limit what serious harm is: for harm of another kind the Act gives no answer (NOTHING).
GIVEN `harm` IS A `Harm I fear` @desc The most serious harm you fear if you return: one of the six instances the Act lists, or harm of another kind
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the harm I fear serious harm question` `harm` MEANS `s 5J(5) -- serious harm` `harm`

-- s 5L: "the person is to be treated as a member of a particular social group (other than the person's family) if: (a) a
-- characteristic is shared by each member of the group; and (b) the person shares, or is perceived as sharing, the
-- characteristic; and (c) any of the following apply: (i) the characteristic is an innate or immutable characteristic;
-- (ii) the characteristic is so fundamental to a member's identity or conscience, the member should not be forced to
-- renounce it; (iii) the characteristic distinguishes the group from society; and (d) the characteristic is not a fear of
-- persecution." An "if" condition: JUST FALSE when it fails (fork F1).
DECLARE `My social group` HAS
    `every member of the group shares a characteristic` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I share the characteristic, or am perceived as sharing it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the characteristic is innate or immutable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the characteristic is so fundamental to identity or conscience that no member should be forced to renounce it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the characteristic distinguishes the group from society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the characteristic is a fear of persecution` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN g IS A `My social group`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5L -- member of a particular social group` g IF
        g's `every member of the group shares a characteristic`
    AND g's `I share the characteristic, or am perceived as sharing it`
    AND (    g's `the characteristic is innate or immutable`
         OR  g's `the characteristic is so fundamental to identity or conscience that no member should be forced to renounce it`
         OR  g's `the characteristic distinguishes the group from society`)
    AND (NOT g's `the characteristic is a fear of persecution`)

@export Am I a member of a particular social group, other than my family (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 5L)? Yes if every member of the group shares a characteristic, you share it or are seen to share it, the characteristic is innate or unchangeable, or so fundamental to identity or conscience that no one should be forced to give it up, or sets the group apart from society, and the characteristic is not itself a fear of persecution.
GIVEN `group` IS A `My social group` @desc Facts about the group you say you belong to (not your family) and its shared characteristic
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a member of a particular social group question` `group` IF `s 5L -- member of a particular social group` `group`

-- s 5LA(1): "effective protection measures are available to the person in a receiving country if: (a) protection
-- against persecution could be provided to the person by: (i) the relevant State; or (ii) a party or organisation,
-- including an international organisation, that controls the relevant State or a substantial part of the territory of
-- the relevant State; and (b) the relevant State, party or organisation ... is willing and able to offer such
-- protection." (2): it "is taken to be able to offer protection ... if: (a) the person can access the protection; and
-- (b) the protection is durable; and (c) in the case of protection provided by the relevant State--the protection
-- consists of an appropriate criminal law, a reasonably effective police force and an impartial judicial system."
-- (1) is an "if" condition: JUST FALSE where (a) or willingness fails. (2) deems ability, without "only": where it
-- fails, whether the protector is otherwise "able" is left open (NOTHING; fork F2).
DECLARE `Protection in my country` HAS
    `protection could be provided by the State, or by a party or organisation controlling the State or a substantial part of its territory` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the protector is willing to offer it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I can access the protection` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the protection is durable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the protector is the State` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the State has an appropriate criminal law, a reasonably effective police force and an impartial judicial system` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN p IS A `Protection in my country`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5LA -- effective protection measures are available` p MEANS
    IF (NOT p's `protection could be provided by the State, or by a party or organisation controlling the State or a substantial part of its territory`)
       OR (NOT p's `the protector is willing to offer it`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF     p's `I can access the protection`
            AND p's `the protection is durable`
            AND (    (NOT p's `the protector is the State`)
                 OR  p's `the State has an appropriate criminal law, a reasonably effective police force and an impartial judicial system`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING

@export Are effective protection measures available to me in my country, so that my fear of persecution is not well-founded (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 5J(2), 5LA)? Yes if the State, or a party or organisation controlling it or much of its territory, could protect you and is willing and able to; it is taken to be able if you can access the protection, it is durable, and (for the State) it consists of an appropriate criminal law, a reasonably effective police force and an impartial judiciary. If those three are not all met, the Act does not say whether the protector is otherwise able (NOTHING).
GIVEN `protection` IS A `Protection in my country` @desc Facts about the protection the State or a controlling party or organisation could give you in your country
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Are effective protection measures available to me question` `protection` MEANS `s 5LA -- effective protection measures are available` `protection`

-- s 5J(3): "A person does not have a well-founded fear of persecution if the person could take reasonable steps to
-- modify his or her behaviour so as to avoid a real chance of persecution ..., other than a modification that would:
-- (a) conflict with a characteristic that is fundamental to the person's identity or conscience; or (b) conceal an
-- innate or immutable characteristic of the person; or (c) ... require the person to ... (i)-(vi)".
DECLARE `Change in my behaviour` IS ONE OF
    `no reasonable change in my behaviour would avoid a real chance of persecution`
    `a reasonable change of another kind would avoid it`
    `a change conflicting with a characteristic fundamental to my identity or conscience`
    `a change concealing an innate or immutable characteristic of mine`
    `altering or concealing my religious beliefs, renouncing a conversion, or ceasing to practise my faith`
    `concealing my race, ethnicity, nationality or country of origin`
    `altering or concealing my political beliefs`
    `concealing a physical, psychological or intellectual disability`
    `entering or remaining in a marriage I oppose, or accepting the forced marriage of a child`
    `altering or concealing my sexual orientation, gender identity or intersex status`

GIVEN `the change` IS A `Change in my behaviour`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5J(3) -- a change in behaviour defeats my fear` `the change` IF
    CONSIDER `the change`
    WHEN `a reasonable change of another kind would avoid it` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Could I be expected to change my behaviour to avoid persecution, so that my fear is not well-founded (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 5J(3))? Only if a reasonable change would avoid a real chance of persecution and is not one the Act protects: a change conflicting with your identity or conscience, hiding an innate or unchangeable characteristic, or altering or hiding your religion, race, ethnicity, nationality, political beliefs, a disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or intersex status, or entering or staying in a marriage you oppose.
GIVEN `change` IS A `Change in my behaviour` @desc The change in your behaviour, if any, that would avoid a real chance of persecution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Could I be expected to change my behaviour question` `change` IF `s 5J(3) -- a change in behaviour defeats my fear` `change`

-- s 5J(1): "the person has a well-founded fear of persecution if: (a) the person fears being persecuted for reasons of
-- race, religion, nationality, membership of a particular social group or political opinion; and (b) there is a real
-- chance that, if the person returned to the receiving country, the person would be persecuted for one or more of the
-- reasons mentioned in paragraph (a); and (c) the real chance of persecution relates to all areas of a receiving
-- country." (2) not if effective protection measures are available (s 5LA); (3) not if a reasonable change of behaviour
-- would avoid it; (4) the reason "must be the essential and significant reason", the persecution "must involve serious
-- harm" and "must involve systematic and discriminatory conduct"; (6) conduct in Australia "is to be disregarded unless
-- the person satisfies the Minister that the person engaged in the conduct otherwise than for the purpose of
-- strengthening the person's claim to be a refugee". A family social group goes to s 5K, which is not encoded (NOTHING).
DECLARE `Reason for the persecution I fear` IS ONE OF
    `race`
    `religion`
    `nationality`
    `membership of a particular social group other than my family`
    `membership of my family as a particular social group`
    `political opinion`
    `none of these reasons`

DECLARE `My fear of persecution` HAS
    `the reason` IS A `Reason for the persecution I fear`
    `the social group` IS A `My social group`
    `there is a real chance I would be persecuted for that reason if I returned` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the real chance relates to all areas of the country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that reason is the essential and significant reason for the persecution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the harm feared` IS A `Harm I fear`
    `the persecution involves systematic and discriminatory conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the protection available` IS A `Protection in my country`
    `the change that would avoid it` IS A `Change in my behaviour`
    `the real chance depends on conduct I engaged in in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I satisfy the Minister I engaged in that conduct otherwise than to strengthen my claim` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN f IS A `My fear of persecution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5J -- the Convention reason` f MEANS
    CONSIDER f's `the reason`
    WHEN `none of these reasons` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `membership of my family as a particular social group` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `membership of a particular social group other than my family` THEN JUST (`s 5L -- member of a particular social group` (f's `the social group`))
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

GIVEN f IS A `My fear of persecution`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5J -- well-founded fear of persecution` f MEANS
    IF     `is no` (`s 5J -- the Convention reason` f)
        OR (NOT f's `there is a real chance I would be persecuted for that reason if I returned`)
        OR (NOT f's `the real chance relates to all areas of the country`)
        OR `is yes` (`s 5LA -- effective protection measures are available` (f's `the protection available`))
        OR `s 5J(3) -- a change in behaviour defeats my fear` (f's `the change that would avoid it`)
        OR (NOT f's `that reason is the essential and significant reason for the persecution`)
        OR (NOT f's `the persecution involves systematic and discriminatory conduct`)
        OR (    f's `the real chance depends on conduct I engaged in in Australia`
            AND (NOT f's `I satisfy the Minister I engaged in that conduct otherwise than to strengthen my claim`))
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF    `is open` (`s 5J -- the Convention reason` f)
            OR `is open` (`s 5J(5) -- serious harm` (f's `the harm feared`))
            OR `is open` (`s 5LA -- effective protection measures are available` (f's `the protection available`))
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@export Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 5J, 5L, 5LA)? You do if you fear persecution for your race, religion, nationality, membership of a particular social group or political opinion; there is a real chance of it in all areas of your country if you return; that reason is the essential and significant reason; the persecution involves serious harm and systematic and discriminatory conduct; effective protection is not available; and no reasonable change of behaviour (of a kind the Act does not protect) would avoid it. Conduct in Australia is disregarded unless you satisfy the Minister it was not to strengthen your claim. NOTHING where the Act leaves the point open (harm outside the listed instances, protection outside s 5LA(2), or a family social group under s 5K, which is not encoded).
GIVEN `fear` IS A `My fear of persecution` @desc Facts about the persecution you fear if you return to your country of nationality (or, if you have none, of former habitual residence)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I have a well-founded fear of persecution question` `fear` MEANS `s 5J -- well-founded fear of persecution` `fear`

-- s 5H(2) and s 36(2C)(a): "the Minister has serious reasons for considering that: (a) the person has committed a crime
-- against peace, a war crime or a crime against humanity, as defined by international instruments prescribed by the
-- regulations; or (b) the person committed a serious non-political crime before entering Australia; or (c) the person
-- has been guilty of acts contrary to the purposes and principles of the United Nations." s 36(1B): an ASIO assessment;
-- s 36(1C), (2C)(b): "the Minister considers, on reasonable grounds" danger to security, or "having been convicted by a
-- final judgment of a particularly serious crime" danger to the community. s 5M: a particularly serious crime
-- "included" a serious Australian offence or a serious foreign offence.
DECLARE `My conviction` IS ONE OF
    `no conviction by final judgment of a particularly serious crime`
    `a serious Australian offence`
    `a serious foreign offence`
    `another particularly serious crime`

DECLARE `Security and crime facts` HAS
    `the Minister has serious reasons for considering I committed a crime against peace, a war crime or a crime against humanity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has serious reasons for considering I committed a serious non-political crime before entering Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has serious reasons for considering I have been guilty of acts contrary to the purposes and principles of the United Nations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ASIO has assessed me to be directly or indirectly a risk to security` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister considers on reasonable grounds I am a danger to Australia's security` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my conviction by final judgment` IS A `My conviction`
    `the Minister considers on reasonable grounds I am a danger to the Australian community` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN s IS A `Security and crime facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister has serious reasons (ss 5H(2), 36(2C)(a))` s IF
       s's `the Minister has serious reasons for considering I committed a crime against peace, a war crime or a crime against humanity`
    OR s's `the Minister has serious reasons for considering I committed a serious non-political crime before entering Australia`
    OR s's `the Minister has serious reasons for considering I have been guilty of acts contrary to the purposes and principles of the United Nations`

GIVEN s IS A `Security and crime facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister considers me a danger (ss 36(1C), 36(2C)(b))` s IF
       s's `the Minister considers on reasonable grounds I am a danger to Australia's security`
    OR (    (NOT (s's `my conviction by final judgment` EQUALS `no conviction by final judgment of a particularly serious crime`))
        AND s's `the Minister considers on reasonable grounds I am a danger to the Australian community`)

-- s 5H(1): "the person is a refugee if the person: (a) in a case where the person has a nationality--is outside the
-- country of his or her nationality and, owing to a well-founded fear of persecution, is unable or unwilling to avail
-- himself or herself of the protection of that country; or (b) in a case where the person does not have a
-- nationality--is outside the country of his or her former habitual residence and owing to a well-founded fear of
-- persecution, is unable or unwilling to return to it." It applies "to a particular person in Australia": outside
-- Australia the section does not reach (NOTHING). (2): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the Minister has serious
-- reasons ..." (JUST FALSE).
DECLARE `My refugee claim` HAS
    `I am in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am outside my country of nationality (or, if I have none, of former habitual residence)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `owing to my fear I am unable or unwilling to seek that country's protection (or, if stateless, to return to it)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my fear` IS A `My fear of persecution`

GIVEN c IS A `My refugee claim`, s IS A `Security and crime facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 5H -- refugee` c s MEANS
    IF (NOT c's `I am in Australia`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF    `the Minister has serious reasons (ss 5H(2), 36(2C)(a))` s
            OR (NOT c's `I am outside my country of nationality (or, if I have none, of former habitual residence)`)
            OR (NOT c's `owing to my fear I am unable or unwilling to seek that country's protection (or, if stateless, to return to it)`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE `s 5J -- well-founded fear of persecution` (c's `my fear`)

@export Am I a refugee under Australian law (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 5H, 5J)? You are if you are in Australia, outside your country of nationality (or, if stateless, of former habitual residence), and owing to a well-founded fear of persecution you are unable or unwilling to seek its protection (or return). Not if the Minister has serious reasons for considering that you committed a crime against peace, a war crime, a crime against humanity or a serious non-political crime before coming to Australia, or acted against the purposes and principles of the United Nations. NOTHING where the Act leaves a point open.
GIVEN `claim` IS A `My refugee claim` @desc Facts about where you are, your country, and the persecution you fear
      `security` IS A `Security and crime facts` @desc What the Minister or ASIO has found or considers about crimes, security and danger (enter FALSE where nothing has been found)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I a refugee question` `claim` `security` MEANS `s 5H -- refugee` `claim` `security`

§§ `s 36(2)(aa), (2A)-(2C) -- complementary protection`

-- s 36(2A): "A non-citizen will suffer significant harm if: (a) ... arbitrarily deprived of his or her life; or (b) the
-- death penalty will be carried out ...; or (c) ... torture; or (d) ... cruel or inhuman treatment or punishment; or (e)
-- ... degrading treatment or punishment." An "if" definition: JUST FALSE for other harm (a plain BOOLEAN).
DECLARE `Harm I face if removed` IS ONE OF
    `arbitrary deprivation of my life`
    `the death penalty carried out on me`
    `torture`
    `cruel or inhuman treatment or punishment`
    `degrading treatment or punishment`
    `harm of some other kind`

GIVEN `the harm` IS A `Harm I face if removed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36(2A) -- significant harm` `the harm` IF
    CONSIDER `the harm`
    WHEN `harm of some other kind` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Is the harm I face if removed "significant harm" (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 36(2A))? Yes if it is arbitrary deprivation of life, the death penalty, torture, cruel or inhuman treatment or punishment, or degrading treatment or punishment; no for harm of any other kind.
GIVEN `harm` IS A `Harm I face if removed` @desc The harm you face if removed from Australia to the country concerned
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the harm I face significant harm question` `harm` IF `s 36(2A) -- significant harm` `harm`

-- s 36(2)(aa): "a non-citizen in Australia (other than a non-citizen mentioned in paragraph (a)) in respect of whom the
-- Minister is satisfied Australia has protection obligations because the Minister has substantial grounds for believing
-- that, as a necessary and foreseeable consequence of the non-citizen being removed from Australia to a receiving
-- country, there is a real risk that the non-citizen will suffer significant harm". (2B): "there is taken not to be a
-- real risk ... if the Minister is satisfied that: (a) it would be reasonable for the non-citizen to relocate to an area
-- of the country where there would not be a real risk ...; or (b) the non-citizen could obtain, from an authority of the
-- country, protection such that there would not be a real risk ...; or (c) the real risk is one faced by the population
-- of the country generally and is not faced by the non-citizen personally." (2C): "taken not to satisfy" (a) serious
-- reasons; (b) danger. The s 36(3) right-to-live-elsewhere rule is applied separately (s 36(3) question).
DECLARE `My complementary protection claim` HAS
    `I am in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has substantial grounds for believing that, as a necessary and foreseeable consequence of my removal, there is a real risk I will suffer the harm` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the harm I face` IS A `Harm I face if removed`
    `the Minister is satisfied it would be reasonable for me to relocate to an area of the country without that risk` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied I could obtain protection from an authority of the country that removes the risk` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied the risk is faced by the population generally and not by me personally` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN c IS A `My complementary protection claim`, s IS A `Security and crime facts`, `I meet s 36(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36(2)(aa) -- complementary protection` c s `I meet s 36(2)(a)` IF
        c's `I am in Australia`
    AND (NOT `I meet s 36(2)(a)`)
    AND c's `the Minister has substantial grounds for believing that, as a necessary and foreseeable consequence of my removal, there is a real risk I will suffer the harm`
    AND `s 36(2A) -- significant harm` (c's `the harm I face`)
    AND (NOT c's `the Minister is satisfied it would be reasonable for me to relocate to an area of the country without that risk`)
    AND (NOT c's `the Minister is satisfied I could obtain protection from an authority of the country that removes the risk`)
    AND (NOT c's `the Minister is satisfied the risk is faced by the population generally and not by me personally`)
    AND (NOT `the Minister has serious reasons (ss 5H(2), 36(2C)(a))` s)
    AND (NOT `the Minister considers me a danger (ss 36(1C), 36(2C)(b))` s)

@export Do I meet the complementary protection criterion for a protection visa (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 36(2)(aa), (2A)-(2C))? You do if you are in Australia, are not owed protection as a refugee, and the Minister has substantial grounds for believing that, as a necessary and foreseeable consequence of your removal, there is a real risk you will suffer significant harm. Not if the Minister is satisfied you could reasonably relocate within the country, could get protection from its authorities, or face only a risk faced by the population generally; and not if the Minister has serious reasons (war crimes and the like) or considers you a danger to security or, after a particularly serious crime, to the community.
GIVEN `claim` IS A `My complementary protection claim` @desc Facts about the harm you face if removed and what the Minister is satisfied of
      `security` IS A `Security and crime facts` @desc What the Minister or ASIO has found or considers about crimes, security and danger (enter FALSE where nothing has been found)
      `refugee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister is satisfied you are owed protection as a refugee (s 36(2)(a)); if so, this criterion is not the one that applies to you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the complementary protection criterion question` `claim` `security` `refugee` IF `s 36(2)(aa) -- complementary protection` `claim` `security` `refugee`

§§ `s 36(3)-(5A) -- a right to live in another country`

-- s 36(3): "Australia is taken not to have protection obligations in respect of a non-citizen who has not taken all
-- possible steps to avail himself or herself of a right to enter and reside in, whether temporarily or permanently ...,
-- any country apart from Australia, including countries of which the non-citizen is a national." (4) not for a country
-- where (a) a well-founded fear of persecution for a Convention reason or (b) the Minister has substantial grounds for
-- believing in a real risk of significant harm; (5) not if a well-founded fear that the country will return the
-- non-citizen to another country where they will be persecuted; (5A) or where the Minister has substantial grounds for
-- believing in a real risk of significant harm in that other country. (6): nationality "determined solely by reference
-- to the law of that country". One other country is asked about at a time.
DECLARE `My right to live in another country` HAS
    `I have a right to enter and reside in a country other than Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have taken all possible steps to avail myself of that right` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have a well-founded fear of persecution in that country for a Convention reason` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has substantial grounds for believing I would face a real risk of significant harm in that country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have a well-founded fear that country would return me to another country` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I would be persecuted in that other country for a Convention reason` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has substantial grounds for believing I would face a real risk of significant harm in that other country` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN r IS A `My right to live in another country`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36(3) -- no protection obligations because of a right elsewhere` r IF
        r's `I have a right to enter and reside in a country other than Australia`
    AND (NOT r's `I have taken all possible steps to avail myself of that right`)
    AND (NOT r's `I have a well-founded fear of persecution in that country for a Convention reason`)
    AND (NOT r's `the Minister has substantial grounds for believing I would face a real risk of significant harm in that country`)
    AND (NOT (    r's `I have a well-founded fear that country would return me to another country`
              AND (    r's `I would be persecuted in that other country for a Convention reason`
                   OR  r's `the Minister has substantial grounds for believing I would face a real risk of significant harm in that other country`)))

@export Does my right to enter and live in another country mean Australia is taken not to owe me protection (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 36(3)-(6))? Yes if you have a right to enter and reside in another country (including one you are a national of, under that country's own law) and have not taken all possible steps to use it. Not if you have a well-founded fear of persecution there, the Minister has substantial grounds for believing you would face a real risk of significant harm there, or you fear that country would send you on to another country where you would be persecuted or face such a risk.
GIVEN `right` IS A `My right to live in another country` @desc Facts about a right you have to enter and live in a country other than Australia, and what you fear there
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a right to live elsewhere stop Australia owing me protection question` `right` IF `s 36(3) -- no protection obligations because of a right elsewhere` `right`

§§ `ss 36, 91WB -- do I meet the Act's criteria for a protection visa`

-- s 36(1A): "An applicant for a protection visa must satisfy: (a) both of the criteria in subsections (1B) and (1C); and
-- (b) at least one of the criteria in subsection (2)." (2)(b), (c): "a non-citizen in Australia who is a member of the
-- same family unit as a non-citizen who: (i) is mentioned in paragraph (a) [or (aa)]; and (ii) holds a protection visa
-- of the same class as that applied for by the applicant". s 91WB(2): "the Minister must not grant the protection visa
-- to the family applicant on the basis of a criterion mentioned in paragraph 36(2)(b) or (c) unless the family
-- applicant applies for the protection visa before the family visa holder is granted a protection visa." "Member of
-- the same family unit" is defined in the Regulations (reg 1.12), not read: asked as a fact. The criteria the
-- Regulations add for each subclass (s 35A(6)(b), Schedule 2) are not encoded.
DECLARE `How my family member holds their protection visa` IS ONE OF
    `I have no family member holding a protection visa`
    `as a refugee (s 36(2)(a))`
    `on complementary protection (s 36(2)(aa))`

DECLARE `My family member's protection visa` HAS
    `I am a member of the same family unit as a person who holds a protection visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how they hold it` IS A `How my family member holds their protection visa`
    `their visa is of the same class as the one I applied for` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I applied before they were granted their visa` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN m IS A `My family member's protection visa`, `the route` IS A `How my family member holds their protection visa`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 36(2)(b), (c), 91WB -- family route` m `the route` IF
        m's `I am a member of the same family unit as a person who holds a protection visa`
    AND m's `how they hold it` EQUALS `the route`
    AND m's `their visa is of the same class as the one I applied for`
    AND m's `I applied before they were granted their visa`

DECLARE `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria` IS ONE OF
    `yes: as a refugee to whom Australia owes protection (s 36(1A), (2)(a))`
    `yes: on complementary protection (s 36(1A), (2)(aa))`
    `yes: as a refugee or on complementary protection, whichever the Minister finds (s 36(1A), (2)(a) or (aa))`
    `yes: as a member of the family unit of a refugee who holds a protection visa (s 36(1A), (2)(b))`
    `yes: as a member of the family unit of a complementary protection visa holder (s 36(1A), (2)(c))`
    `no: ASIO has assessed me as a risk to security (s 36(1B))`
    `no: the Minister considers me a danger to security or, after a particularly serious crime, to the community (s 36(1C))`
    `no: I meet none of the criteria in s 36(2)`
    `not covered: whether I am a refugee turns on a point the Act leaves open`

GIVEN `in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN, `refugee claim` IS A `My refugee claim`, `complementary claim` IS A `My complementary protection claim`, `right elsewhere` IS A `My right to live in another country`, `family` IS A `My family member's protection visa`, `security` IS A `Security and crime facts`
GIVETH A `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria`
`s 36 -- the Act's criteria` `in Australia` `refugee claim` `complementary claim` `right elsewhere` `family` `security` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `security`'s `ASIO has assessed me to be directly or indirectly a risk to security`
              THEN `no: ASIO has assessed me as a risk to security (s 36(1B))`
           IF `the Minister considers me a danger (ss 36(1C), 36(2C)(b))` `security`
              THEN `no: the Minister considers me a danger to security or, after a particularly serious crime, to the community (s 36(1C))`
           IF `is yes` `the refugee answer` AND `owed protection`
              THEN `yes: as a refugee to whom Australia owes protection (s 36(1A), (2)(a))`
           IF `is no` `the refugee answer` AND `owed protection` AND `s 36(2)(aa) -- complementary protection` `complementary claim` `security` FALSE
              THEN `yes: on complementary protection (s 36(1A), (2)(aa))`
           IF `is open` `the refugee answer` AND `owed protection` AND `s 36(2)(aa) -- complementary protection` `complementary claim` `security` FALSE
              THEN `yes: as a refugee or on complementary protection, whichever the Minister finds (s 36(1A), (2)(a) or (aa))`
           IF `in Australia` AND `s 36(2)(b), (c), 91WB -- family route` `family` `as a refugee (s 36(2)(a))`
              THEN `yes: as a member of the family unit of a refugee who holds a protection visa (s 36(1A), (2)(b))`
           IF `in Australia` AND `s 36(2)(b), (c), 91WB -- family route` `family` `on complementary protection (s 36(2)(aa))`
              THEN `yes: as a member of the family unit of a complementary protection visa holder (s 36(1A), (2)(c))`
           IF `is open` `the refugee answer` AND `owed protection`
              THEN `not covered: whether I am a refugee turns on a point the Act leaves open`
           OTHERWISE `no: I meet none of the criteria in s 36(2)`
    WHERE
        `the refugee answer` MEANS `s 5H -- refugee` `refugee claim` `security`
        `owed protection` MEANS NOT (`s 36(3) -- no protection obligations because of a right elsewhere` `right elsewhere`)

@export Do I meet the criteria the Migration Act itself sets for a protection visa (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 36, 91WB)? You must not be assessed by ASIO as a security risk, must not be considered by the Minister a danger to security or (after a particularly serious crime) to the community, and must meet one of: refugee, complementary protection, or member of the same family unit as a refugee or complementary protection visa holder (for these two, you must have applied before they were granted their visa, and their visa must be of the class you applied for). A right to live in another country you have not used can take away protection. The further criteria in the Migration Regulations for each protection visa subclass are not part of this answer.
GIVEN `in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are in Australia
      `refugee claim` IS A `My refugee claim` @desc Facts about your country and the persecution you fear
      `complementary claim` IS A `My complementary protection claim` @desc Facts about the harm you face if removed and what the Minister is satisfied of
      `right elsewhere` IS A `My right to live in another country` @desc Facts about any right you have to enter and live in another country (enter FALSE for the first fact if you have none)
      `family` IS A `My family member's protection visa` @desc Facts about a family member who holds a protection visa, if any
      `security` IS A `Security and crime facts` @desc What the Minister or ASIO has found or considers about crimes, security and danger (enter FALSE where nothing has been found)
GIVETH A `Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria`
`Do I meet the Act's protection visa criteria question` `in Australia` `refugee claim` `complementary claim` `right elsewhere` `family` `security` MEANS
    `s 36 -- the Act's criteria` `in Australia` `refugee claim` `complementary claim` `right elsewhere` `family` `security`

-- s 36A(1): "In considering a valid application for a protection visa ..., the Minister must consider and make a record
-- of whether the Minister is satisfied" of the refugee or complementary protection criteria; (2) "before deciding
-- whether to grant or refuse", before other criteria, and "without regard to subsections 36(2C) and (3)". (3): "Subsection
-- (1) does not apply if: (a) the non-citizen ... is a member of the same family unit as another non-citizen ... who holds
-- a protection visa of the same class ...; and (b) the family applicant's application ... was made before the family
-- visa holder was granted their visa; and (c) the family visa holder is a non-citizen mentioned in paragraph 36(2)(a) or
-- (aa)." The record is the "protection finding" that s 197C(4) relies on.
@export Must the Minister first decide, and record, whether I am owed protection as a refugee or on complementary protection, before deciding my protection visa (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 36A)? Yes for a valid application, before any other criterion and without regard to the exclusions in s 36(2C) and (3); that record can later stop your removal to the country concerned (s 197C). Not if you applied as a family member of a refugee or complementary protection visa holder whose visa is of the class you applied for, before they were granted it.
GIVEN `valid application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a valid application for a protection visa
      `family` IS A `My family member's protection visa` @desc Facts about a family member who holds a protection visa, if any
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Minister first record whether I am owed protection question` `valid application` `family` IF
        `valid application`
    AND (NOT (   `s 36(2)(b), (c), 91WB -- family route` `family` `as a refugee (s 36(2)(a))`
              OR `s 36(2)(b), (c), 91WB -- family route` `family` `on complementary protection (s 36(2)(aa))`))

§§ `ss 5AA, 46A, 48A, 48B, 91C-91F, 91J-91L -- can I make a valid application`

-- s 5AA(1): "a person is an unauthorised maritime arrival if: (a) the person entered Australia by sea: (i) at an excised
-- offshore place at any time after the excision time for that place; or (ii) at any other place at any time on or after
-- the commencement of this section; and (b) the person became an unlawful non-citizen because of that entry; and (c) the
-- person is not an excluded maritime arrival." (1A): born in the migration zone to a parent who is then an unauthorised
-- maritime arrival because of (1), and not an Australian citizen at birth. (3): "A person is an excluded maritime arrival
-- if the person: (a) is a New Zealand citizen who holds and produces a New Zealand passport that is in force; or (b) is
-- a non-citizen who: (i) holds and produces a passport that is in force; and (ii) is ordinarily resident on Norfolk
-- Island; or (c) is included in a prescribed class of persons."
DECLARE `How I came to Australia` HAS
    `I entered Australia by sea at a place and time s 5AA(1)(a) covers` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I became an unlawful non-citizen because of that entry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a New Zealand citizen who held and produced a New Zealand passport in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I held and produced a passport in force and am ordinarily resident on Norfolk Island` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am in a class of persons the regulations prescribe as excluded maritime arrivals` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was born in the migration zone` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a parent of mine was an unauthorised maritime arrival under s 5AA(1) when I was born` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was an Australian citizen at birth` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN h IS A `How I came to Australia`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5AA -- unauthorised maritime arrival` h IF
       (    h's `I entered Australia by sea at a place and time s 5AA(1)(a) covers`
        AND h's `I became an unlawful non-citizen because of that entry`
        AND (NOT h's `I am a New Zealand citizen who held and produced a New Zealand passport in force`)
        AND (NOT h's `I held and produced a passport in force and am ordinarily resident on Norfolk Island`)
        AND (NOT h's `I am in a class of persons the regulations prescribe as excluded maritime arrivals`))
    OR (    h's `I was born in the migration zone`
        AND h's `a parent of mine was an unauthorised maritime arrival under s 5AA(1) when I was born`
        AND (NOT h's `I was an Australian citizen at birth`))

@export Am I an "unauthorised maritime arrival" (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 5AA)? Yes if you entered Australia by sea (at an excised offshore place after its excision time, or anywhere else since the section began), became an unlawful non-citizen because of that entry, and are not an excluded maritime arrival (a New Zealand citizen with a New Zealand passport, a passport holder ordinarily resident on Norfolk Island, or a prescribed class). Also yes if you were born in Australia to a parent who was then an unauthorised maritime arrival, and were not an Australian citizen at birth.
GIVEN `arrival` IS A `How I came to Australia` @desc Facts about how you (or, if you were born here, your parent) came to Australia
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an unauthorised maritime arrival question` `arrival` IF `s 5AA -- unauthorised maritime arrival` `arrival`

-- s 46A(1): "An application for a visa is not a valid application if it is made by an unauthorised maritime arrival
-- who: (a) is in Australia; and (b) either: (i) is an unlawful non-citizen; or (ii) holds a bridging visa or a temporary
-- protection visa, or a temporary visa of a kind ... prescribed". (1A): not if the applicant holds, or as a lawful
-- non-citizen has ever held, a safe haven enterprise visa, the visa applied for is prescribed, and the prescribed work,
-- study or social security requirements are met. (2): the Minister may, in the public interest, by written notice
-- determine that (1) does not apply to an application for a visa of a specified class; (2A) for a period if it says so.
-- The Minister has no duty to consider doing so (s 46A(7)).
DECLARE `My s 46A facts` HAS
    `I am an unauthorised maritime arrival` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am an unlawful non-citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold a bridging visa, a temporary protection visa, or a temporary visa of a kind prescribed for s 46A(1)(b)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold a safe haven enterprise visa, or have held one and am a lawful non-citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the visa I apply for is prescribed for s 46A(1A)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I meet the work, study or social security requirements prescribed for s 46A(1A)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has determined under s 46A(2) that the bar does not apply to me for this class of visa, and the determination is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN f IS A `My s 46A facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 46A -- my application is not valid` f IF
        f's `I am an unauthorised maritime arrival`
    AND f's `I am in Australia`
    AND (    f's `I am an unlawful non-citizen`
         OR  f's `I hold a bridging visa, a temporary protection visa, or a temporary visa of a kind prescribed for s 46A(1)(b)(ii)`)
    AND (NOT (    f's `I hold a safe haven enterprise visa, or have held one and am a lawful non-citizen`
              AND f's `the visa I apply for is prescribed for s 46A(1A)(b)`
              AND f's `I meet the work, study or social security requirements prescribed for s 46A(1A)(c)`))
    AND (NOT f's `the Minister has determined under s 46A(2) that the bar does not apply to me for this class of visa, and the determination is in effect`)

@export As an unauthorised maritime arrival, does the Act stop me making a valid application for a visa, including a protection visa (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 46A)? Yes if you are in Australia and are an unlawful non-citizen or hold a bridging visa, a temporary protection visa or another prescribed temporary visa. Not if you hold (or, lawfully here, have held) a safe haven enterprise visa, are applying for a prescribed visa and meet the prescribed work, study or social security requirements; and not if the Minister has personally lifted the bar for you for that class of visa (the Minister has no duty to consider doing so).
GIVEN `facts` IS A `My s 46A facts` @desc Facts about how you arrived, your visa status, and any determination the Minister has made for you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does s 46A stop me applying question` `facts` IF `s 46A -- my application is not valid` `facts`

-- s 48A(1), (1AA): a non-citizen who, "while in the migration zone", made (or had made on their behalf) an application
-- for a protection visa that was refused "(whether or not the application has been finally determined)" "may not make a
-- further application for a protection visa, or have a further application for a protection visa made on his or her
-- behalf, while the non-citizen is in the migration zone"; (1AA)(b) whether or not they knew of or understood it because of
-- mental impairment or being a minor. (1B): one whose protection visa was cancelled likewise. (1C): whatever the grounds.
-- (1A), (1AB): after a removal or attempted removal and return under s 42(2A)(d), (da) or (e), the person is "taken to
-- have been continuously in the migration zone". s 48B(1): the Minister may, in the public interest, by written notice
-- determine that s 48A "does not apply to prevent an application ... in the period starting when the notice is given and
-- ending at the end of the seventh working day after the day on which the notice is given".
-- Not in the migration zone: "while" (JUST FALSE). No refusal and no cancellation: s 48A does not reach (JUST FALSE, fork
-- F3). Left the migration zone since, other than as (1A), (1AB) deem: the text does not say the bar ends (NOTHING, fork F4).
DECLARE `My s 48A facts` HAS
    `I am in the migration zone` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a protection visa application made by me or for me while I was in the migration zone has been refused` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a protection visa I held was cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have left the migration zone since, other than by a removal or attempted removal after which s 48A(1A) or (1AB) treats me as having stayed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has given me a notice under s 48B and I apply within its period` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN f IS A `My s 48A facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48A -- no further protection visa application` f MEANS
    IF     (NOT f's `I am in the migration zone`)
        OR (    (NOT f's `a protection visa application made by me or for me while I was in the migration zone has been refused`)
            AND (NOT f's `a protection visa I held was cancelled`))
        OR f's `the Minister has given me a notice under s 48B and I apply within its period`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF f's `I have left the migration zone since, other than by a removal or attempted removal after which s 48A(1A) or (1AB) treats me as having stayed`
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@export My protection visa application was refused, or my protection visa was cancelled: does the Act stop me making another protection visa application while I am in Australia (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 48A, 48B)? Yes, whatever new grounds you have, and even if the earlier application was made for you and you did not know of or understand it because you were a minor or had a mental impairment. A removal or attempted removal followed by return does not break your stay. The bar is lifted only by a notice the Minister personally gives you, and only for an application within the period it allows (the Minister has no duty to consider it). If you have left Australia since in another way, the Act does not say whether the bar still applies (NOTHING).
GIVEN `facts` IS A `My s 48A facts` @desc Facts about your earlier protection visa application or visa, where you are, and any notice from the Minister
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does s 48A stop me applying again question` `facts` MEANS `s 48A -- no further protection visa application` `facts`

-- ss 48B(1), 91F(1)(a), 91L(1): the notice lifts the bar for an application "in the period starting when the notice is
-- given and ending at the end of the seventh working day after the day on which [or "that"] the notice is given".
@export The Minister has given me a notice lifting a bar on my visa application: what is the last day I can apply within its period (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 48B(1), 91F(1)(a), 91L(1))? The end of the seventh working day after the day the notice was given. Enter the public holidays in the place concerned; Saturdays and Sundays are skipped.
GIVEN `notice given on` IS A DATE @desc The day the Minister's notice was given to you
      `public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc The public holidays in the place concerned that fall in the next three weeks (an empty list if none)
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day to apply after the Minister's notice question` `notice given on` `public holidays` MEANS
    `working days after` 7 `notice given on` `public holidays`

-- ss 91C, 91D, 91E: the Subdivision applies to a non-citizen "in Australia" who "is covered by: (i) the CPA; or (ii) an
-- agreement, relating to persons seeking asylum, between Australia and a country that is ... a safe third country in
-- relation to the non-citizen", and "is not excluded by the regulations". A safe third country is one "prescribed as a
-- safe third country" with which the non-citizen "has a prescribed connection" (s 91D(1)). s 91E: if the non-citizen
-- "applies, or purports to apply, for a protection visa" then, subject to s 91F, "(a) if the non-citizen has not been
-- immigration cleared at that time--neither that application nor any other application made by the non-citizen for a
-- visa is a valid application; or (b) if the non-citizen has been immigration cleared at that time--neither that
-- application nor any other application made by the non-citizen for a protection visa is a valid application."
DECLARE `My safe third country facts` HAS
    `I am in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am covered by the CPA, or by an asylum agreement between Australia and a country prescribed as a safe third country with which I have a prescribed connection` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulations exclude me from Subdivision AI` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I apply or purport to apply for a protection visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have been immigration cleared` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has given me a notice under s 91F and I apply within its period` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `What s 91E does to my applications` IS ONE OF
    `s 91E does not affect my applications`
    `the Minister's s 91F notice lets my application be valid`
    `no visa application I make at this time is valid (s 91E(a))`
    `no protection visa application I make at this time is valid (s 91E(b))`

GIVEN f IS A `My safe third country facts`
GIVETH A `What s 91E does to my applications`
`s 91E -- safe third country bar` f MEANS
    IF     (NOT f's `I am in Australia`)
        OR (NOT f's `I am covered by the CPA, or by an asylum agreement between Australia and a country prescribed as a safe third country with which I have a prescribed connection`)
        OR f's `the regulations exclude me from Subdivision AI`
        OR (NOT f's `I apply or purport to apply for a protection visa`)
    THEN `s 91E does not affect my applications`
    ELSE IF f's `the Minister has given me a notice under s 91F and I apply within its period`
         THEN `the Minister's s 91F notice lets my application be valid`
         ELSE IF f's `I have been immigration cleared`
              THEN `no protection visa application I make at this time is valid (s 91E(b))`
              ELSE `no visa application I make at this time is valid (s 91E(a))`

@export I am covered by the Comprehensive Plan of Action or by an asylum agreement with a safe third country: can I make a valid protection visa application (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 91C-91F)? If you apply for a protection visa while in Australia and covered (and not excluded by the regulations), that application is invalid, and so is any other protection visa application you make at that time; if you have not been immigration cleared, every visa application you make at that time is invalid. A notice the Minister personally gives you can lift this for applications within the period it allows.
GIVEN `facts` IS A `My safe third country facts` @desc Facts about your coverage by the CPA or a safe third country agreement, your application and immigration clearance
GIVETH A `What s 91E does to my applications`
`Does a safe third country stop me applying question` `facts` MEANS `s 91E -- safe third country bar` `facts`

-- ss 91J, 91K: the Subdivision applies to a non-citizen in Australia who "(a) holds a temporary safe haven visa; or (b)
-- has not left Australia since ceasing to hold a temporary safe haven visa", but "does not apply to an unauthorised
-- maritime arrival or a transitory person"; such a non-citizen's application "for a visa (other than a temporary safe
-- haven visa) ... is not a valid application", subject to a s 91L notice.
DECLARE `My temporary safe haven facts` HAS
    `I am in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold a temporary safe haven visa, or have not left Australia since I stopped holding one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am an unauthorised maritime arrival or a transitory person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am applying for another temporary safe haven visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has given me a notice under s 91L and I apply within its period` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN f IS A `My temporary safe haven facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 91K -- my application is not valid` f IF
        f's `I am in Australia`
    AND f's `I hold a temporary safe haven visa, or have not left Australia since I stopped holding one`
    AND (NOT f's `I am an unauthorised maritime arrival or a transitory person`)
    AND (NOT f's `I am applying for another temporary safe haven visa`)
    AND (NOT f's `the Minister has given me a notice under s 91L and I apply within its period`)

@export I hold, or have held, a temporary safe haven visa: does the Act stop me applying for any other visa, including a protection visa (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 91J-91L)? Yes while you are in Australia holding one, or if you have not left Australia since it ended, unless you are applying for another temporary safe haven visa or the Minister has personally given you a notice lifting the bar for that period. Unauthorised maritime arrivals and transitory persons are dealt with by other sections instead.
GIVEN `facts` IS A `My temporary safe haven facts` @desc Facts about your temporary safe haven visa and the visa you are applying for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a temporary safe haven visa stop me applying question` `facts` IF `s 91K -- my application is not valid` `facts`

§§ `ss 91V, 91W, 91WA -- while my application is decided`

-- s 91V(1): the Minister or an officer "may ... request the applicant to make an oral statement, on oath or
-- affirmation, to the effect that the information is true." (2): if the applicant "refuses or fails to comply" and was
-- warned when asked "that the Minister may draw an inference unfavourable to the applicant's credibility", the Minister
-- "may draw any reasonable inference unfavourable to the applicant's credibility". (3): likewise if the applicant
-- complies but "the Minister has reason to believe that, because of: (i) the manner in which the applicant complied
-- ...; or (ii) the applicant's demeanour ... the applicant was not sincere". The warning is needed only in (2).
DECLARE `My oral statement` HAS
    `I was asked to make an oral statement on oath or affirmation that my information is true` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I refused or failed to make it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `when asked I was warned the Minister may draw an unfavourable inference about my credibility if I refused or failed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has reason to believe, from the manner of my statement or my demeanour, that I was not sincere` IS A BOOLEAN

@export May the Minister hold it against my credibility that I did not, or did not sincerely, swear that the information in my protection visa application is true (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 91V(1)-(3))? Yes if you were asked to make an oral statement on oath or affirmation and refused or failed after being warned of this; or if you made it but the Minister has reason to believe, from how you made it or your demeanour, that you were not sincere. The inference must be reasonable.
GIVEN `statement` IS A `My oral statement` @desc Facts about the request to confirm your information on oath or affirmation and what happened
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May the Minister doubt my credibility question` `statement` IF
        `statement`'s `I was asked to make an oral statement on oath or affirmation that my information is true`
    AND (   (    `statement`'s `I refused or failed to make it`
             AND `statement`'s `when asked I was warned the Minister may draw an unfavourable inference about my credibility if I refused or failed`)
         OR (    (NOT `statement`'s `I refused or failed to make it`)
             AND `statement`'s `the Minister has reason to believe, from the manner of my statement or my demeanour, that I was not sincere`))

-- s 91W(2): "The Minister must refuse to grant the protection visa to the applicant if: (a) the applicant has been given
-- a request under subsection (1) [to produce documentary evidence of identity, nationality or citizenship]; and (b) the
-- applicant refuses or fails to comply with the request, or produces a bogus document in response to the request; and
-- (c) the applicant does not have a reasonable explanation ...; and (d) when the request was made, the applicant was
-- given a warning ... that the Minister cannot grant the protection visa" if so. (3): "does not apply if the Minister is
-- satisfied that the applicant: (a) has a reasonable explanation ...; and (b) either: (i) produces documentary evidence
-- ...; or (ii) has taken reasonable steps to produce such evidence."
-- s 91WA(1): "must refuse ... if: (a) the applicant provides a bogus document as evidence of the applicant's identity,
-- nationality or citizenship; or (b) the Minister is satisfied that the applicant: (i) has destroyed or disposed of
-- documentary evidence ...; or (ii) has caused such documentary evidence to be destroyed or disposed of." (2): not if the
-- Minister is satisfied of a reasonable explanation and that the applicant provides evidence or has taken reasonable steps.
-- One "reasonable explanation" input serves (2)(c), (3)(a) and 91WA(2)(a): the person states the explanation and
-- whether the Minister accepts it.
DECLARE `My identity documents` HAS
    `I was asked to produce documentary evidence of my identity, nationality or citizenship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I refused or failed to comply, or produced a bogus document in response` IS A BOOLEAN
    `when asked I was warned the Minister cannot grant the visa if I did so` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I provided a bogus document as evidence of my identity, nationality or citizenship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied I destroyed or disposed of such evidence, or caused that` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister is satisfied I have a reasonable explanation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have produced documentary evidence of my identity, nationality or citizenship, or taken reasonable steps to` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN d IS A `My identity documents`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 91W -- refusal for not producing identity documents` d IF
        d's `I was asked to produce documentary evidence of my identity, nationality or citizenship`
    AND d's `I refused or failed to comply, or produced a bogus document in response`
    AND (NOT d's `the Minister is satisfied I have a reasonable explanation`)
    AND d's `when asked I was warned the Minister cannot grant the visa if I did so`

GIVEN d IS A `My identity documents`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 91WA -- refusal for bogus or destroyed identity documents` d IF
        (   d's `I provided a bogus document as evidence of my identity, nationality or citizenship`
         OR d's `the Minister is satisfied I destroyed or disposed of such evidence, or caused that`)
    AND (NOT (    d's `the Minister is satisfied I have a reasonable explanation`
              AND d's `I have produced documentary evidence of my identity, nationality or citizenship, or taken reasonable steps to`))

@export Must my protection visa be refused because of my identity documents (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 91W, 91WA)? Yes if you were asked to produce evidence of your identity, nationality or citizenship, were warned that the visa cannot be granted otherwise, and refused, failed or produced a bogus document without a reasonable explanation. Yes also if you gave a bogus identity document, or the Minister is satisfied you destroyed or got rid of such evidence, unless the Minister is satisfied you have a reasonable explanation and you have produced evidence of your identity or taken reasonable steps to.
GIVEN `documents` IS A `My identity documents` @desc Facts about any request for identity documents, what you produced, and what the Minister is satisfied of
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my visa be refused over identity documents question` `documents` IF
       `s 91W -- refusal for not producing identity documents` `documents`
    OR `s 91WA -- refusal for bogus or destroyed identity documents` `documents`

§§ `ss 494B, 494C, 379A, 379C; reg 2.16(3) -- when I am taken to have received the decision`

-- reg 2.16(3): "The Minister must notify an applicant of a decision to refuse to grant a visa by one of the methods
-- specified in section 494B". s 494C (the Minister) and s 379C (the ART): by hand, "when it is handed"; to another person
-- at the address, "when it is handed to the other person"; by prepaid post, "(a) if the document was dispatched from a
-- place in Australia to an address in Australia--7 working days (in the place of that address) after the date of the
-- document; or (b) in any other case--21 days after the date of the document"; by fax, email or other electronic means,
-- "at the end of the day on which the document is transmitted"; by online account (s 494C(6) only), "at the end of the
-- day on which it is made available". s 379A has no online account method: NOTHING for the ART.
-- s 494C(7), 379C(7) (a later actual receipt after an error in the method) are not encoded.
DECLARE `Who gave me the document` IS ONE OF
    `the Minister or the Department`
    `the ART`

DECLARE `How the document was given` IS ONE OF
    `handed to me`
    `handed to another person at my last residential or business address`
    `sent by prepaid post or other prepaid means from Australia to an address in Australia`
    `sent by prepaid post or other prepaid means in any other case`
    `sent by fax, email or other electronic means`
    `made available in my online account`

GIVEN `who` IS A `Who gave me the document`, `how` IS A `How the document was given`, `the day` IS A DATE, `public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ss 494C, 379C -- taken to have received` `who` `how` `the day` `public holidays` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how`
    WHEN `sent by prepaid post or other prepaid means from Australia to an address in Australia` THEN JUST (`working days after` 7 `the day` `public holidays`)
    WHEN `sent by prepaid post or other prepaid means in any other case` THEN JUST (`plain days after` 21 `the day`)
    WHEN `made available in my online account` THEN
        IF `who` EQUALS `the ART`
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE JUST `the day`
    OTHERWISE JUST `the day`

@export When am I taken to have received a decision or other document from the Minister or the ART (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 494C, 379C; Migration Regulations 1994 reg 2.16(3))? Handed to you or to another adult at your address: that day. Emailed, faxed or sent electronically, or (from the Minister) put in your online account: the end of that day. Posted from Australia to an Australian address: 7 working days after the date on the document, at that address; posted in any other case: 21 days after the date on the document. A refusal of a visa must be given by one of these methods. The ART has no online account method (NOTHING).
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who gave me the document` @desc Who gave you the document: the Minister (or the Department) or the ART
      `how` IS A `How the document was given` @desc How the document was given to you
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day it was handed over, transmitted or made available; for post, the date written on the document
      `public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc For post within Australia, the public holidays at your address in the three weeks after the date on the document (an empty list if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`When am I taken to have received the document question` `who` `how` `the day` `public holidays` MEANS
    `ss 494C, 379C -- taken to have received` `who` `how` `the day` `public holidays`

§§ `ss 338A, 347, 347A, 348; reg 4.31B -- review by the ART (if my visa is refused or cancelled)`

-- s 338A(1): reviewable protection decisions include "(c) a decision to refuse to grant a protection visa, other than a
-- decision that was made relying on: (i) subsection 5H(2), or 36(1B) or (1C); or (ii) paragraph 36(2C)(a) or (b)"; "(d)
-- a decision to cancel a protection visa, other than a decision that was made because of: (i) subsection 5H(2) or
-- 36(1C); or (ii) an assessment by [ASIO] that the holder ... is directly or indirectly a risk to security ...; or (iii)
-- paragraph 36(2C)(a) or (b)"; "(e) a decision under subsection 197D(2)". (2): "The following decisions are not
-- reviewable protection decisions: (a) decisions in relation to which the Minister has issued a conclusive certificate
-- under section 339; (b) any decision to cancel a protection visa that is made personally by the Minister; (c) decisions
-- made in relation to a non-citizen who is not physically present in the migration zone when the decision is made."
-- s 347A(4), (5): an application "may only be made by the non-citizen who is the subject of the decision" and "only ...
-- by a non-citizen who is physically present in the migration zone when the application for review is made".
-- (a), (b) (decisions before 1 September 1994) are not encoded. Another decision is outside s 338A (NOTHING: it may be a
-- reviewable migration decision under s 338, not encoded). "Other than" a decision on an excluded ground: JUST FALSE
-- (fork F5).
DECLARE `The decision about me` IS ONE OF
    `a refusal to grant me a protection visa`
    `a cancellation of my protection visa`
    `a decision under s 197D(2) that I am no longer owed protection`
    `another decision`

DECLARE `The ground of the decision` IS ONE OF
    `none of the grounds below`
    `s 5H(2): the Minister's serious reasons (war crimes, serious non-political crime, acts against the United Nations)`
    `s 36(1B) or an ASIO assessment that I am a risk to security`
    `s 36(1C): the Minister considers me a danger to security or the community`
    `s 36(2C)(a) or (b)`

DECLARE `My review facts` HAS
    `the decision` IS A `The decision about me`
    `the ground` IS A `The ground of the decision`
    `the Minister has issued a conclusive certificate for the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister personally cancelled my protection visa` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was physically in the migration zone when the decision was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am physically in the migration zone now` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN r IS A `My review facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 338A, 347A -- I can apply to the ART` r MEANS
    IF r's `the decision` EQUALS `another decision`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF    r's `the Minister has issued a conclusive certificate for the decision`
            OR (r's `the decision` EQUALS `a cancellation of my protection visa` AND r's `the Minister personally cancelled my protection visa`)
            OR (NOT r's `I was physically in the migration zone when the decision was made`)
            OR (    (NOT (r's `the decision` EQUALS `a decision under s 197D(2) that I am no longer owed protection`))
                AND (NOT (r's `the ground` EQUALS `none of the grounds below`)))
            OR (NOT r's `I am physically in the migration zone now`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

@export Can I apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal (ART) for review of the decision refusing or cancelling my protection visa, or deciding I am no longer owed protection (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 338A, 347A)? Yes for a refusal or cancellation of a protection visa, or a s 197D(2) decision, if you were in Australia when it was made and are in Australia when you apply. Not if the Minister issued a conclusive certificate, personally cancelled the visa, or the decision relied on war crimes or similar serious reasons, an ASIO security assessment, or your being a danger (s 5H(2), 36(1B), (1C), (2C)). Only you, the person the decision is about, can apply. Other decisions are outside these sections (NOTHING).
GIVEN `review` IS A `My review facts` @desc Facts about the decision, what it relied on, and where you were and are
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I apply to the ART question` `review` MEANS `ss 338A, 347A -- I can apply to the ART` `review`

-- s 347(3): "An application must be made: (a) if the applicant is in immigration detention on the day the applicant is
-- notified of the decision--within 14 days after the day the applicant is notified of the decision; or (b)
-- otherwise--within 28 days after the day the applicant is notified of the decision." (5): s 19 of the ART Act (the
-- Tribunal may extend the period) "does not apply". s 348(1) and its note: "The ART has no jurisdiction to review a
-- decision if the application for review is not properly made."
GIVEN `detained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 347(3) -- days allowed` `detained` MEANS
    IF `detained`
    THEN 14
    ELSE 28

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Protection party` `Protection step`
`s 347(3) -- I must apply to the ART in time` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I, the applicant`
    MUST `apply to the ART for review`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I, the applicant` BECAUSE "no application within the s 347(3) period: the ART cannot extend it (s 347(5)) and has no jurisdiction over an application not properly made (s 348)"

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 347(3) -- an application on this day is in time` `the days allowed` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 347(3) -- I must apply to the ART in time` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `I, the applicant` `apply to the ART for review` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export By when must I apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal (ART) for review of a protection visa decision (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 347(3), (5))? Within 28 days after the day you are notified of the decision, or within 14 days if you were in immigration detention on that day. The ART cannot extend this period. Use the day you are taken to have received the decision (see the question on receiving documents). The day worked out is the last day as counted under the Act; if it falls on a Saturday, a Sunday or a public holiday, the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 36(2) may let you apply on the next working day, which this question does not work out.
GIVEN `notified on` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified of the decision (the day you are taken to have received it)
      `detained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in immigration detention on the day you were notified
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I apply to the ART question` `notified on` `detained` MEANS
    `plain days after` (`s 347(3) -- days allowed` `detained`) `notified on`

DECLARE `Am I in time to apply to the ART` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I applied within the period (s 347(3))`
    `not yet late: the period has not ended`
    `out of time: the ART cannot extend the period (s 347(5)) and cannot review the decision (s 348)`

@export Am I in time to apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal (ART) for review of my protection visa decision (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 347(3), (5), 348)? You must apply within 28 days after the day you were notified (14 days if you were then in immigration detention). The ART cannot extend the time, and has no power to review a decision on a late application. The last day is not moved for weekends or public holidays here (see the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 36(2)).
GIVEN `notified on` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified of the decision (the day you are taken to have received it)
      `detained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in immigration detention on the day you were notified
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already applied to the ART
      `applied on` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied (if you have not, any date; it is not used)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date (used when you have not yet applied)
GIVETH A `Am I in time to apply to the ART`
`Am I in time to apply to the ART question` `notified on` `detained` `I have applied` `applied on` `today` MEANS
    IF `s 347(3) -- an application on this day is in time` (`s 347(3) -- days allowed` `detained`) (`plain days between` `notified on` `the day of applying`)
    THEN IF `I have applied`
         THEN `yes: I applied within the period (s 347(3))`
         ELSE `not yet late: the period has not ended`
    ELSE `out of time: the ART cannot extend the period (s 347(5)) and cannot review the decision (s 348)`
    WHERE
        `the day of applying` MEANS
            IF `I have applied`
            THEN `applied on`
            ELSE `today`

-- reg 4.31B(1): "The prescribed fee for an application for review by the ART of a reviewable protection decision is
-- $2,151." (subject to annual indexation from 1 July 2025 under regs 4.31BA, 4.31BB: the indexed fee is an input).
-- (3): "No fee is payable if the ART remits a matter to which the decision relates with a permissible order under
-- regulation 4.33." (3AA): none for a decision referred, or a proceeding continued, under the ART transitional items.
-- (3A): no further fee after a court remits the matter to the ART, if a fee was paid. (4): combined applications, "only
-- 1 fee is payable".
DECLARE `My ART fee facts` HAS
    `the ART remitted the matter with a permissible order under reg 4.33` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my review was referred or continued under the ART transitional provisions (Schedule 16 items 35-37)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a court remitted the matter to the ART and I already paid the fee` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my application was combined with others and the one fee has been paid for all of us` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the fee as indexed for the current year (0 if not known)` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN f IS A `My ART fee facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 4.31B -- the ART fee` f MEANS
    IF    f's `the ART remitted the matter with a permissible order under reg 4.33`
       OR f's `my review was referred or continued under the ART transitional provisions (Schedule 16 items 35-37)`
       OR f's `a court remitted the matter to the ART and I already paid the fee`
       OR f's `my application was combined with others and the one fee has been paid for all of us`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF f's `the fee as indexed for the current year (0 if not known)` GREATER THAN 0
         THEN f's `the fee as indexed for the current year (0 if not known)`
         ELSE 2151

@export How much must I pay for the Administrative Review Tribunal's review of my protection visa decision (Migration Regulations 1994 reg 4.31B)? $2,151 (indexed each 1 July from 2025 by the consumer price index; enter the current figure if you know it). Nothing if the ART sends the matter back to the Minister with a permissible order, for reviews carried over under the ART transitional provisions, again after a court sends the matter back if you already paid, or for a combined application whose one fee is already paid.
GIVEN `fee facts` IS A `My ART fee facts` @desc Facts about how your review ended and the current indexed fee
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much is the ART fee question` `fee facts` MEANS `reg 4.31B -- the ART fee` `fee facts`

-- reg 4.31B(2): "The fee must be paid within the 7-day period beginning on the day when: (a) if the ART's decision is
-- given to the applicant orally--the applicant is taken, under subsection 368(7) of the Act, to have been notified of that
-- decision [on the day it is given orally]; or (b) otherwise--the applicant is taken, under section 379C of the Act, to
-- have received the notification of that decision." The period includes its first day: day 0 to day 6.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Protection party` `Protection step`
`reg 4.31B(2) -- I must pay the ART fee in time` MEANS
    PARTY `I, the applicant`
    MUST `pay the ART review fee`
    WITHIN 6
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I, the applicant` BECAUSE "the fee was not paid within the 7-day period beginning on the day I was notified of the ART's decision (reg 4.31B(2))"

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 4.31B(2) -- a payment on this day is in time` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `reg 4.31B(2) -- I must pay the ART fee in time` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `I, the applicant` `pay the ART review fee` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export By when must I pay the Administrative Review Tribunal fee for review of my protection visa decision (Migration Regulations 1994 reg 4.31B(2); Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 368(7), 379C)? Within the 7-day period beginning on the day you are notified of the ART's decision: the day it was given to you orally, or otherwise the day you are taken to have received the written notification. The day of notification counts as the first of the 7 days.
GIVEN `notified on` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified of the ART's decision (given orally, or taken to have received the written notification)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I pay the ART fee question` `notified on` MEANS `plain days after` 6 `notified on`

@export Have I paid the Administrative Review Tribunal fee for my protection review in time (Migration Regulations 1994 reg 4.31B(2))? In time if paid within the 7-day period beginning on the day you were notified of the ART's decision.
GIVEN `notified on` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified of the ART's decision
      `paid on` IS A DATE @desc The day you paid the fee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I paid the ART fee in time question` `notified on` `paid on` IF
        `is no later than` `notified on` `paid on`
    AND `reg 4.31B(2) -- a payment on this day is in time` (`plain days between` `notified on` `paid on`)

§§ `ss 197C, 197D -- can I be sent to the country I fear (if I am to be removed)`

-- s 197C(3): "section 198 does not require or authorise an officer to remove an unlawful non-citizen to a country if:
-- (a) the non-citizen has made a valid application for a protection visa that has been finally determined; and (b) in
-- the course of considering the application, a protection finding within the meaning of subsection (4), (5), (6) or (7)
-- was made for the non-citizen with respect to the country (whether or not the visa was refused or was granted and has
-- since been cancelled); and (c) none of the following apply: (i) the decision in which the protection finding was made
-- has been quashed or set aside; (ii) a decision made under subsection 197D(2) in relation to the non-citizen is complete
-- ...; (iii) the non-citizen has asked the Minister, in writing, to be removed to the country." (7A): only the last
-- finally determined application counts. (9): a withdrawn request is taken not to have been made.
-- s 197C(1), (2): otherwise non-refoulement obligations are "irrelevant" to removal under s 198.
DECLARE `My removal facts` HAS
    `my last valid protection visa application has been finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in it a protection finding was made for me with respect to the country (s 197C(4)-(7))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the decision with that finding has been quashed or set aside` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a s 197D(2) decision that I am no longer owed protection is complete` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have asked the Minister in writing to remove me to that country, and not withdrawn the request` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Does the Act stop me being removed to the country where I was found to be owed protection (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) s 197C(3)-(9))? Yes if your last valid protection visa application has been finally determined, a protection finding was made for you about that country in it (whether the visa was refused, or granted and later cancelled), the decision with the finding has not been quashed or set aside, no decision that you are no longer owed protection is complete, and you have not asked in writing (without withdrawing) to be removed there. Otherwise the duty to remove you arises whether or not Australia owes you protection.
GIVEN `removal` IS A `My removal facts` @desc Facts about your protection visa application, any protection finding, and what has happened since
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act stop my removal to that country question` `removal` IF
        `removal`'s `my last valid protection visa application has been finally determined`
    AND `removal`'s `in it a protection finding was made for me with respect to the country (s 197C(4)-(7))`
    AND (NOT `removal`'s `the decision with that finding has been quashed or set aside`)
    AND (NOT `removal`'s `a s 197D(2) decision that I am no longer owed protection is complete`)
    AND (NOT `removal`'s `I have asked the Minister in writing to remove me to that country, and not withdrawn the request`)

-- s 197D(6): a decision under (2) "is complete if any of the following apply: (a) the period within which an application
-- for review of the decision under Part 5 can be made has ended without an application for review having been properly
-- made; (b) an application for review of the decision under Part 5 was properly made within the period but has been
-- withdrawn; (c) the decision is affirmed (or taken to have been affirmed) on review by the ART." The period is s 347(3).
@export The Minister has decided I am no longer owed protection: is that decision "complete", so that it no longer stops my removal (Migration Act 1958 (Cth) ss 197D(6), 347(3))? Yes once your time to apply to the ART (28 days after you were notified, or 14 if you were then in immigration detention) has ended without a proper application; or once you withdraw an application made in time; or once the ART affirms the decision.
GIVEN `notified on` IS A DATE @desc The day you were notified of the decision that you are no longer owed protection
      `detained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were in immigration detention on that day
      `applied in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you properly applied to the ART for review within the time allowed
      `withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have withdrawn that application
      `affirmed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the ART has affirmed the decision (or it is taken to have been affirmed)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the decision that I am no longer owed protection complete question` `notified on` `detained` `applied in time` `withdrawn` `affirmed` `today` IF
       (    (NOT `applied in time`)
        AND `is later than` `today` (`By when must I apply to the ART question` `notified on` `detained`))
    OR (`applied in time` AND `withdrawn`)
    OR (`applied in time` AND `affirmed`)
